{"tool_name":"gcua","contents":["oeb","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"gcua","home":"http://gcua.schoedl.de","summary":"Differences in codon usage preference among organisms lead to a variety of problems concerning heterologous gene expression but can be overcome by rational gene design and gene synthesis. The gcua tool displays the codon quality either in codon usage frequency values or relative adaptiveness values.","addition_date":"2017-05-16T12:57:19Z","last_update_date":"2018-12-10T12:58:56Z","tool_type":["Web application"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:gcua","credit":[{"email":"thomas.gcua@schoedl.de","name":"Thomas Sch\u00f6dl","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"http://gcua.schoedl.de/contact.html"}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://gcua.schoedl.de/seqoverallex.html"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Codon usage analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0286"},{"term":"Codon usage bias calculation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2962"},{"term":"Codon usage bias plotting","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2963"},{"term":"Codon usage table comparison","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0285"},{"term":"Codon usage table generation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0284"},{"term":"Protein sequence analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2479"}]}],"name":"Graphical Codon Usage Analyser","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"ELIXIR-EE","publication":[{"metadata":{"abstract":"The program General Codon Usage Analysis (GCUA) has been developed for analysing codon and amino acid usage patterns. Availability: ftp://ftp.nhm.ac.uk/pub/gcua. Freely available for acedemic use, commercial users should contact the author. Contact: J.McInerney@@@nhm.ac.uk.","authors":[{"name":"McInerney J.O."}],"citationCount":125,"date":"1998-01-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"GCUA: General codon usage analysis"},